            <ArticleTitle>A possible adenine nucleotide storage form in normal and ischaemic rat heart.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>7-12</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Perfusion of Langendorff rat hearts with [14C]adenosine yields an acid-insoluble, radioactive product whose concentration falls during ischaemia. The properties of the substance show that it is a polyribonucleotide. It is suggested that it may be mitochondrial poly A acting as a storage form of adenine nucleotides.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
